<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Claudius Florimund Mercy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1666–1734</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Claude Florimond de Mercy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> Florimund Mercy was a Lorraine-born <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> field marshal who served as the first governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timisoara">Temeswar</a> from 1716 until 1734. He rebuilt Temeswar as a baroque fortress town, drained marshes, dug the Bega canal and brought in German, Italian and other settlers to farm the region and grow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>. He was killed at the Battle of Parma in 1734 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-polish-succession">War of the Polish Succession</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/claudius-florimund-mercy.jpg" alt="Claudius Florimund Mercy" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Claude_Florimond_de_Mercy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
